<report>
<title>Kendall's rank correlation</title>
<line></line>
<line><in>sample_1</in> vs. <in>sample_2</in></line>
<line>Observations per sample = <in>obs</in></line>
<line>Concordant pairs  =  <in>con</in></line>
<line>Discordant pairs  =  <in>dis</in></line>
<line>Tied pairs = <in>tie</in></line>
<line>Kendall's score = <in>s</in>   (standard error = <inu>ses</inu>)</line>
<line>Gamma = <inu>gam</inu></line>
<line></line>
<line>Kendall's <in>tb</in>  = <inu>tau</inu></line>
<line><ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% CI = <inu>ll</inu> to <inu>ul</inu></ci></line>
<line></line>
<line><u>Approximate tests<in>adj</in></u></line>
<block name="smallsample">
<line><warn>Sample size too small for reliable inference from z, use exact test</warn></line>
</block>
<line>z = <inu>kz</inu></line>
<line><pval>Upper side <inp>p_u</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: concordance)</line>
<line><pval>Lower side <inp>p_l</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: discordance)</line>
<line><pval>Two sided <inp>p_2</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: dependence)</line>
<line></line>
<line>z (continuity corrected) = <inu>kzcc</inu></line>
<line><pval>Upper side <inp>p_ucc</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: concordance)</line>
<line><pval>Lower side <inp>p_lcc</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: discordance)</line>
<line><pval>Two sided <inp>p_2cc</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: dependence)</line>
<line></line>
<line><u>Exact test<in>adjexact</in></u></line>
<line><pval>Upper side <inp>p_uexact</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: concordance)</line>
<line><pval>Lower side <inp>p_lexact</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: discordance)</line>
<line><pval>Two sided <inp>p_2exact</inp></pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: dependence)</line>
</report>
